From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaviya-RM6 <exclaim_plethora227@simplelogin.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:51:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: keep the core clock and its MMCX vote consistent

When the last CRTC is disabled, dpu_core_perf_crtc_update() asks for a
core clock rate of 0. dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, 0) drops the performance
state vote but leaves the MDP core clock running at its last rate
(460 MHz on the REDMAGIC 6). Nothing else votes on MMCX there, so the
rail drops under the running MDP: the MDP TOP registers still answer,
but every core block (CTL, SSPP, ...) stops responding. The next enable
reads CTL_START in dpu_kms_wait_flush() before the new rate is set, the
access hangs the bus and the SoC resets with no log. Turning the screen
off and on again rebooted the phone every time.

Park at the lowest OPP instead of 0, so the clock drops to 200 MHz and
keeps a matching vote. Runtime PM drops the vote while the DPU is
suspended and restores it on resume as before.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_core_perf.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_core_perf.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_core_perf.c
@@ -395,6 +395,26 @@
 		trace_dpu_core_perf_update_clk(kms->dev, !crtc->enabled, clk_rate);
 
 		clk_rate = min(clk_rate, kms->perf.max_core_clk_rate);
+
+		/*
+		 * A rate of 0 drops the performance state vote but leaves the
+		 * core clock running at its last rate. Without another MMCX
+		 * voter the rail then drops under the running MDP, and the next
+		 * register access (e.g. CTL at the following enable) hangs the
+		 * bus. Park at the lowest OPP instead, which keeps the clock
+		 * and the vote consistent.
+		 */
+		if (!clk_rate) {
+			unsigned long min_rate = 0;
+			struct dev_pm_opp *opp;
+
+			opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_ceil(&kms->pdev->dev, &min_rate);
+			if (!IS_ERR(opp)) {
+				dev_pm_opp_put(opp);
+				clk_rate = min_rate;
+			}
+		}
+
 		ret = dev_pm_opp_set_rate(&kms->pdev->dev, clk_rate);
 		if (ret) {
 			DPU_ERROR("failed to set core clock rate %llu\n", clk_rate);
--
2.47.0
